        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\pm2$; quadratic; $x^2$; negative.",
          "worked": "Let $u=x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2+5u-36&=0\\\\(u-4)(u+9)&=0\\\\u&=4\\text{ or }-9\\end{align*}$$\nFor $u=4$, $x^2=4$, so $x=\\pm2$. For $u=-9$, $x^2=-9$ has no real solution.\nThe substitution makes the equation quadratic. Since $u$ represents $x^2$, substitute back to find $x$. A real square cannot be negative.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
